---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Chess Tournament Calendar — About" description="What this site is, where the data comes from, and how it works." lang="en" currentPath="about">
  <h1 class="page-title">About Chess Tournament Calendar</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      Finding out what chess tournaments are coming up, anywhere in the world and at any level, usually means
      checking several federation sites by hand. This site pulls that into one place.
    </p>

    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      Tournament listings are gathered automatically from <a href="https://chess-results.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">chess-results.com</a>,
      with rating data from <a href="https://ratings.fide.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ratings.fide.com</a>.
      The site refreshes every 6 hours. We don't organize any of these tournaments ourselves, and we don't take
      entries or payments; every listing links out to the tournament's own registration page or website when one
      exists. A tournament stays listed as long as it keeps showing up in the data behind the scenes: a single
      missed or failed update won't pull a real tournament off the site, since it takes several consecutive misses
      before we assume it's concluded or cancelled and drop it from the upcoming list. A small number of tournaments
      are hand-picked and pinned as featured instead, usually partner events we want to give extra visibility.
    </p>
    <p>
      This process gets things wrong sometimes: a date, a location, a tournament that's been cancelled without us
      noticing yet. If you spot an error, or you run a tournament and want something fixed, use the
      <a href="/contact">contact form</a> and it'll reach a person directly.
    </p>

    <h2>Who runs this</h2>
    <p>
      Chess Tournament Calendar is run on a non-profit basis from Finland. You can reach us any time through the
      <a href="/contact">contact form</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
